media IMAGE photo_notebook_page.webp by=sekar unlock=photo_notebook_page [if clue_sekar_notebook == true]
  id: buat jaga2 kalau halamannya gue sobek
  en: just in case i tear the page out
  clue notebook_page

narration [if clue_sekar_notebook == true]
  id: Halaman yang disobek itu. Kertas yang sama yang gue gosok pake pensil hari pertama. Sekarang kebaca semuanya.
  en: The torn-out page. The same page I rubbed with a pencil on the first day. Now all of it is readable.
narration [if clue_sekar_notebook == true]
  id: "Jangan percaya Tasya soal sponsor. Dia bukan jahat, dia butuh uang."
  en: "Don't trust Tasya on the sponsor. She isn't bad, she needs the money."
narration [if clue_sekar_notebook == true]
  id: Bukan "jangan percaya Tasya". Jangan percaya Tasya soal satu hal. Sekar masih belain dia, bahkan di catatan yang cuma buat dirinya sendiri.
  en: Not "don't trust Tasya". Don't trust Tasya about one thing. Sekar was still defending her, even in notes meant only for herself.

narration [if clue_sekar_notebook != true]
  id: Ada satu foto halaman buku catatan, tapi buram, kefoto miring. Dinda ngegedein layarnya, nyipitin mata.
  en: There's one photo of a notebook page, but it's blurry, taken at an angle. Dinda zooms in, squinting.
narration [if clue_sekar_notebook != true]
  id: "Kak Sekar pernah bilang ke gue soal Tasya," katanya pelan. "Tasya bukan orang jahat. Dia cuma lagi butuh duit banget. Nyokapnya sakit."
  en: "Sekar told me something about Tasya once," she says quietly. "Tasya isn't a bad person. She just really needs money. Her mom's sick."

narration
  id: "Satu yang gue bawa ke mana-mana."{w} Perekam Zoom-nya. Kartu memorinya. Dia bawa buktinya bareng dia.
  en: "One I carry everywhere."{w} Her Zoom recorder. Its memory card. She took the proof with her.

-> d4_choice


@conversation d4_choice chapter="Hari 4" chapter.en="Day 4" title="Atap" title.en="The Roof"
@scene VN bg=bg_sekar_roof_dusk.webp music=bgm_low_tide.mp3 ambience=amb_kampung_day.mp3 day=4 time=18:10

stage
  show raka:neutral left
  show dinda:neutral right

narration
  id: Magrib lagi dari tiga masjid. Crane-crane reklamasi udah nyalain lampu merahnya, satu-satu, kayak mata.
  en: The call to prayer again, from three mosques. The reclamation cranes have switched on their red lights, one by one, like eyes.

dinda:neutral [right] [if heard_silent_call == true]
  id: Telepon semalem. Lo bilang ada bunyi klik dua kali. Itu apa?
  en: Last night's call. You said there were two clicks. What were they?
raka:sad [left] [if heard_silent_call == true]
  id: Waktu gue masih jadi editornya, kita rekaman di tempat-tempat berisik. Pasar, dermaga, demo. Nggak bisa ngomong, nggak bisa teriak.
  en: Back when I was still her editor, we recorded in loud places. Markets, piers, protests. You couldn't talk, couldn't shout.
raka:sad [if heard_silent_call == true]
  id: Jadi kita bikin kode. Klik tombol rekam sekali artinya "tunggu". Dua kali artinya "gue aman, lanjut rekam".
  en: So we made up a code. One click of the record button meant "wait". Two clicks meant "I'm okay, keep rolling".
dinda:crying [if heard_silent_call == true]
  id: Dia aman.
  en: She's okay.
raka:sad [if heard_silent_call == true]
  id: Dia pake kode yang cuma gue yang ngerti. Setahun gue nggak ngomong sama dia, dan dia masih pake kode kita.
  en: She used a code only I would understand. A year I didn't speak to her, and she still used our code.
narration [if heard_silent_call == true]
  id: Dinda nangis tanpa suara, mukanya ditutupin lengan sweater Sekar. Gue biarin. Gue juga.
  en: Dinda cries without a sound, her face hidden in the sleeve of Sekar's sweater. I let her. I do too.

dinda:neutral [right]
  id: Oke. Kita punya dua jalan.
  en: Okay. We have two ways in.
dinda:neutral
  id: Satu, dermaga. Pak Hendra tahu sesuatu. Kapalnya, telepon tanpa suara itu, ombak sama genset.
  en: One, the pier. Pak Hendra knows something. His boat, that silent call, the waves and the generator.
dinda:neutral
  id: Dua, orang-orangnya. Tasya ditelepon orang PT. Bima ngomong sesuatu ke bosnya. Didit dapet nomor HP ini dari Bima. Ada yang nyambung di situ.
  en: Two, the people. Tasya got a call from the company. Bima said something to his boss. Didit got this phone's number from Bima. Something connects there.
raka:neutral [left]
  id: Kita bisa dua-duanya.
  en: We could do both.
dinda:angry
  id: Didit tahu semester gue, Ka. Kita nggak punya waktu buat dua-duanya.
  en: Didit knows what semester I'm in, Ka. We don't have time for both.

choice ROUTE_LEAN by=dinda:neutral
  id: Ke mana dulu?
  en: Where first?
? Ke dermaga. Cari Pak Hendra lagi. | The pier. Find Pak Hendra again.
  value harbor
  set route_lean "harbor"
? Ke orang-orangnya. Tasya dan Bima. | The people. Tasya and Bima.
  value network
  set route_lean "network"

dinda:hopeful [if ROUTE_LEAN == 'harbor']
  id: Dermaga. Kalau Kak Sekar ketemu narsumnya di laut, jawabannya ada di laut.
  en: The pier. If Sekar met her source at sea, the answer is at sea.
raka:determined [if ROUTE_LEAN == 'harbor' && trust_hendra > 0]
  id: Dia bilang "jaga adiknya". Dia nggak bakal bilang gitu kalau dia nggak peduli.
  en: He said "look after her sister". He wouldn't say that if he didn't care.
raka:worried [if ROUTE_LEAN == 'harbor' && trust_hendra <= 0]
  id: Dia nutup pintu waktu itu. Kali ini gue harus ngetok dengan cara yang bener.
  en: He shut me out last time. This time I have to knock the right way.
dinda:neutral [if ROUTE_LEAN == 'network']
  id: Orang-orangnya. Tasya bukan jahat, Bima bukan jahat. Tapi salah satu dari mereka yang bikin Didit tahu.
  en: The people. Tasya isn't bad, Bima isn't bad. But one of them is how Didit found out.
raka:determined [if ROUTE_LEAN == 'network']
  id: Dan orang yang ngerasa bersalah biasanya pengen ngaku. Mereka cuma butuh orang yang mau dengerin.
  en: And people who feel guilty usually want to confess. They just need someone who'll listen.

narration
  id: Kita duduk di dak sampai gelap. Dinda nyenderin kepalanya ke bahu gue, cuma sebentar, kayak lupa.
  en: We sit on the roof until it's dark. Dinda leans her head on my shoulder, just for a moment, like she forgot not to.

